s:
Since two intersecting lines within plane $\alpha$ are parallel to two lines within plane $\beta$, it implies that the two intersecting lines are parallel to $\beta$, thus $\alpha \parallel \beta$, statement (a) is correct;  
According to the theorem for determining when a line is parallel to a plane, statement (b) is correct;  
Since there is a line within $\alpha$ perpendicular to $l$, this line does not necessarily have to be perpendicular to the plane, thus $\alpha$ and $\beta$ are not necessarily perpendicular, statement (c) is incorrect;  
According to the theorem for determining when a line is perpendicular to a plane, if a line is perpendicular to two intersecting lines within the plane, the line is perpendicular to the plane, thus statement (d) is incorrect;  
Therefore, the correct choice is $\boxed{\text{B}}$.

